<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">French colonial empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as French Empire, First Empire, Second Empire</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The French colonial empire comprised the overseas territories ruled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. The first empire, built from the seventeenth century in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, was largely lost by 1815; the second, built from the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a> in 1830, covered large parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indochina">Indochina</a> before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/decolonisation">decolonisation</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire.jpg" alt="French colonial empire" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Royal_Standard_of_the_King_of_France.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Pius VII returned in 1800, but in 1809 Napoleon annexed the remaining states to the <b>French Empire</b> and the pope was held captive until 1814.</blockquote><a href="/empire/papal-states">Papal States · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Instead he built up his own power, his forces massacred mixed-race opponents in Port-au-Prince in April 1848, and on 26 August 1849 he proclaimed himself Emperor Faustin I, ending the republic and creating the <b>Second Empire</b> of Haiti.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-haiti-1806-1849">Republic of Haiti (1806-1849) · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>On 31 January 1808 Marshal Auguste Marmont proclaimed the abolition of the republic, and its territory was soon incorporated into the Illyrian Provinces of the <b>French Empire</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-ragusa">Republic of Ragusa · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>It became the official anthem of the <b>French Empire</b>.</blockquote><a href="/songs/chant-du-depart">Le Chant du départ</a></li><li><blockquote>He had written an earlier version in September 1870 to greet the Third Republic declared after the fall of the <b>Second Empire</b>, and meant the song to be sung to the tune of &quot;La Marseillaise&quot;.</blockquote><a href="/songs/the-internationale">The Internationale</a></li><li><blockquote>Within months France was defeated, the <b>Second Empire</b> fell and the German Empire was proclaimed at Versailles.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/july-19">19 July in history</a></li></ul></section>
